  "page_meta": {
    "image_alt": "HumanityOS: software to unite humanity in peaceful harmony.",
    "accord": "Read the Humanity Accord, the shared principles HumanityOS is built on, one document at a time.",
    "admin": "The admin dashboard for the people who run this server: activity, members, alerts and the server's settings.",
    "apps": "HumanityOS's own tools, free programs from their makers, and real-world help services, gathered in one place.",
    "bugs": "Report a problem with HumanityOS, or vote on the reports others have made so the worst get fixed first.",
    "calculator": "A free calculator with basic math, scientific functions and unit conversion, right in your browser.",
    "calendar": "Your own calendar for the day, the week or the month, kept in this browser.",
    "chat": "Talk with people on HumanityOS in open rooms, in direct messages sealed end to end, and on calls, with no sign-up.",
    "civilization": "Live numbers from the HumanityOS community: people, resources, infrastructure and decisions at a glance.",
    "crafting": "Look up every recipe in the HumanityOS game: what it takes, what it makes and where to make it.",
    "dev": "Tools for the people building HumanityOS: the asset browser, icon tests, the component showcase and the theme's colours.",
    "donate": "Two ways to support HumanityOS: give to the maintainer directly, or to the nonprofit Sponsor-a-Can, where a gift can be tax-deductible.",
    "download": "Download the free HumanityOS desktop app: one program that holds the everyday tools, the game and the server.",
    "files": "See and share files on this server: what members have published for everyone, and the files you keep here yourself.",
    "guilds": "Find or start a guild: a group of people working together on something they care about.",
    "hi": "Free, practical guides for growing food, collecting water and making power. Start with one.",
    "home": "The ideal closed-loop homestead for one person: every loop and part that keeps food, water, power and air going, honestly sized.",
    "how_to": "Step-by-step guides for real life and for HumanityOS: what you need, the steps to tick off, and what to do if something goes wrong.",
    "humanity": "The mission and the shared civic tools: how we decide together, what we agree to, who we are and how the work is funded.",
    "identity": "Prove who you are without giving away more than you choose: your key, what others vouch for, your trust score, and whether you are a person or an AI.",
    "inventory": "Your own list of what you own, sorted by where it is (on you, in your bag or at home), saved in this browser.",
    "library": "Everything HumanityOS has written, in one place: free guides, the Humanity Accord, and a dictionary for every term.",
    "maps": "Zoom from your own street out to the whole galaxy: the real Earth, the planets and the stars on one map.",
    "market": "A market for buying, selling and offering services to other people, like a flea market everyone can use.",
    "mission": "Why HumanityOS exists: end poverty through self-sufficiency, protect the freedoms that keep power honest, and keep it all public domain forever.",
    "notes": "Write notes or keep a daily log in your browser; a note you lock with a passphrase is encrypted so only you can read it.",
    "onboarding": "Learn to secure clean water, grow your own food and make your own power through step-by-step chains of tasks.",
    "ops": "A behind-the-scenes look at how the app is running in your browser right now: its connection, its storage and what it has saved.",
    "profile": "Your profile: set your name, picture and bio, choose who sees each part, and show the skills you have.",
    "recovery": "Recovery through trusted people: choose friends who each keep a locked piece of your recovery phrase, help a friend back in, or ask yours for help.",
    "roadmap": "Where HumanityOS is going, by theme: what is done, what is being built and what is planned next.",
    "rules": "The rules for united-humanity.us, who moderates it, what powers they hold, and how to appeal a decision.",
    "settings": "Change how HumanityOS looks, sounds and works, and keep your identity safe in your vault.",
    "tasks": "Your own to-do list, kept on your devices, beside this server's shared board of community tasks.",
    "technical": "One open source Rust program builds a desktop app and a federated server: identity from a 24-word recovery phrase, sealed direct messages and its own call relay.",
    "trade": "Trade items directly with another player; nothing changes hands until both of you agree.",
    "wallet": "A wallet you control for sending, receiving and keeping crypto on Solana, made from the same recovery phrase as your identity.",
    "wallet_guide": "A beginner's guide to the HumanityOS crypto wallet: sending, receiving, swapping, backing up, and the words it uses.",
    "watch": "Watch live streams broadcast from the HumanityOS desktop app to this server.",
    "web": "A reading list of useful websites, sorted by topic, plus your own bookmarks.",
    "widgets": "A safe playground for the interface's building blocks, where nothing you press does anything real."
  },
